 The fixture engine exists only for deterministic tests, examples, and offline contract demonstrations. It is not a model and does not infer a score.
 
+## Exact task-revision identity
+
+`task_id` is a logical administrative label. Schema-1.1 requests also require
+`task_revision_fingerprint`, the complete SHA-256 digest of the exact normalized
+task content. The digest participates in `request_fingerprint`; it is never
+derived from the logical ID or metadata. Domain adapters must propagate the
+content-owning artifact's fingerprint explicitly. See
+[`scoring_task_revision_identity.md`](scoring_task_revision_identity.md) for the
+legacy migration and calibration-axis contract.
+
 ## Status semantics
 
 - `scored`: contains one score category declared by the exact bound rubric and no terminal reason.
